'. The frozen tests only cover omitted sections with no surrounding blank lines, so they do not catch this. Smallest fix: when skip_empty drops a section, also drop one blank line that the template holds right after it, by collapsing the line break that follows the omitted section's standalone END_SECTION line, so that two neighbours never get more blank lines between them than the template held between any one pair. Alternatively, have the lead record in the contract that the doubled blank line is accepted.

serves.scenario:
In '{{SECTION "O"}}
{{SECTION "I"}}x{{END_SECTION}}
more
{{SECTION "J"}}y{{END_SECTION}}' only O is unclosed, yet the syntax-error points at line 4 (J), a section that is properly closed. The latestSection heuristic in validateBlocks is what the frozen test 'unclosed inner SECTION is located at the inner tag' needs, and the token structure alone cannot tell that case apart from this one. A fix would therefore conflict with the frozen test; this is for the lead to settle.

